  "term": "bufotenin",
  "definition": "Bufotenin is a hallucinogenic substance related to serotonin that occurs in some frogs or toads, mushrooms, plants, and mammals. In mental health contexts, it is noted for being found especially in the brains, plasma, and urine of people with schizophrenia and for its misuse as a psychedelic.",
